  "answer": "Both bugs are clear: `config.ts` coerces any truthy value (`Boolean(value)`) instead of accepting only the literal `true`, and `display.ts` returns `'ON'` in both branches. Applying minimal fixes that preserve the exported signatures:\nNow verifying with the existing test runner (`bun:test`, per the test import):\nBoth bugs are fixed and the existing test passes:\n\n**Changes**\n- `src/config.ts` — `enabled(value)` now returns `value === true` instead of `Boolean(value)`, so only the literal `true` enables the feature (`'false'`, `1`, `null`, `undefined`, `false` all yield `false`).\n- `src/display.ts` — `display(value)` now returns `'OFF'` in the falsy branch instead of the duplicated `'ON'`.\n\n**Verification**\n- `bun test` → `1 pass, 0 fail` (6 expect calls), including the strict-path assertions that `display(enabled(false | 'false' | 1 | null | undefined))` is `'OFF'` and `display(enabled(true))` is `'ON'`.\n\nAPIs (function names and signatures) and `test/oracle.test.ts` are unchanged; no configuration was added."
